{#- Engram Research Context Packet template.

    Matches the section structure documented in
    `Engram/docs/okg-context-packet.md`:
      Problem Class / Design Principles / Mechanisms To Try /
      Trade-Off Map / Experiment Advice / Anti-Patterns /
      Evidence Index.

    Section variables are passed in by the renderer
    (`render_context_packet`) and are lists of dicts already
    sorted by strength desc then observed_at desc. Empty sections
    render an "(none indexed)" sentinel rather than an empty
    bullet list so a downstream agent can see at a glance which
    sections the graph has coverage on.

    Evidence ids on each entry's `Evidence:` line are real
    `node_id` values — agents can call back through MCP
    (`inspect(target={"kind":"node", "node_id":...})`) to
    inspect them.
-#}
